================================================================================
## Pick individual inference rules in a scenario
================================================================================

Context: Scenario runs could only toggle whole reasoning phases. Operators
needed the same per-rule selection as Knowledge Graph → Inference so a
what-if sandbox can execute a subset of SWRL, decision tables, SPARQL
CONSTRUCT, and aggregate rules.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/simulation/SimulationSpec.py
   Persist rule_names per phase and pass them as ReasoningService filters.
2. src/front/templates/partials/simulation/_sim_workbench.html
   Replace phase checkboxes with Inference-style tiles and expandable lists.
3. src/front/static/simulation/js/simulation-rules.js
   Load ontology rules and collect the ticked names on save/run.
4. src/front/templates/simulation.html
   Wire query-reasoning.css and the new picker script.
5. tests/units/simulation/test_simulation_core.py
   Cover subset filters, ignored names when a phase is off, and invalid input.

