## Split the scenario workbench into three tabs
================================================================================

Context: The scenario editor stacked identity, scope, sandbox objects,
hypothetical facts, and reasoning on one long page. Operators asked for the
same card-integrated tab pattern used elsewhere: General, Hypothetical
facts, and Reasoning, with Save / Run / Reset staying on the header.

Changes:

1. src/front/templates/partials/simulation/_sim_workbench.html
   Card-integrated ob-tabs: General (scenario, scope, artifacts), Hypothetical
   facts (wizard + table, patch-count badge), Reasoning (phase tiles).
2. tests/units/front/test_simulation_page_contract.py
   Assert the three tab buttons, pane ids, and that Save/Run stay outside panes.
3. docs/user-guide.md
   Document the Scenario editor as the three-tab flow.

